From: Try FydeOS contributors
Subject: [PATCH] virglrenderer: build without Venus again

Applies after Try Omarchy's virglrenderer 0001-0005 on
cmspam/winq-emu-virglrenderer.

The fork queries the Venus capset from vkr directly, which only links with
-Dvenus=true. Fedora 43's mingw64 Vulkan headers (1.4.321) are older than
the fork's Venus protocol, so this runtime builds without Venus; keep the
upstream proxy query (a zero-size capset) for that case.

--- a/src/virglrenderer.c
+++ b/src/virglrenderer.c
@@ -575,7 +575,11 @@
       break;
    case VIRTGPU_DRM_CAPSET_VENUS:
       *max_ver = 0;
+#ifdef ENABLE_VENUS
       *max_size = vkr_get_capset(NULL, state.flags);
+#else
+      *max_size = proxy_get_capset(cap_set, NULL);
+#endif
       break;
    case VIRTGPU_DRM_CAPSET_DRM:
       *max_ver = 0;
